 ## Background
-Conditional NeRF was introduced in the paper "CLIP-NeRF: Text-and-Image Driven Manipulation of Neural Radiance Fields" [S1]. It builds on the idea of neural radiance fields by conditioning them on external inputs like text. The deformation network is inspired by Nerfies [S1], but differs by using a shape code to deform the global volume field of various object instances rather than a single fixed object [S1]. The Face Prior Model variant was introduced in "Preface: A Data-driven Volumetric Prior for Few-shot Ultra High-resolution Face Synthesis" [S2], extending MipNeRF360 with conditioning inputs [S2].
